# Files Fern must not modify or delete when regenerating this repo.
#
# Fern owns the SDK source and its ci.yml, and prunes anything it did not generate — it
# reads this file from the pull request's base branch, so an entry only protects a file
# once it is on main.
#
# publish-main.yml is hand-written: it releases whop_sdk when a merge to main lands a
# lib/whop_sdk/version.rb that is not yet on RubyGems. It is meant to be the only publish
# path, and it authenticates with the RUBYGEMS_API_KEY secret.
#
# The Fern Ruby generator also writes a tag-triggered `gem push` job into the ci.yml it
# owns, which fires on any refs/tags/* push — including the tag publish-main.yml creates —
# and holds id-token: write while it runs `bundle install`. It authenticates with RubyGems
# trusted publishing, so it is inert as long as no trusted publisher naming ci.yml exists.
# Neutralising it properly means adding .github/workflows/ci.yml here alongside a
# hand-written lint/test copy; see sdks/fern/README.md in whop-monorepo.
.github/workflows/publish-main.yml
